1|0@playark^1438830575#ctt631m:JasePearson$:Loss is inevitable buddy, I know it's pretty bullshit how it happened but you should view it as a learning experience and not as a big deal that'll make you quit the game. Remember it's only early access, it's nowhere close to being done. Take what you know and build upon it. I don't expect you to build a massive enclosure to defend your base, but instead, slowly build outwards. Start off with a 2x2 metal building, use stone to build up outer layers, doesn't matter if they can kill it off quickly, just use it as a guide to build metal over. Expand to a 4x4, with your central 2x2 being the loot room and the rest of it being walls and turrets. If you're a two man crew, it won't be that difficult, while I'm part of a small guild, I have my own emergency building that I'm turning into a mountain fortress just incase our home is destroyed. I advise taking a mountain (such as the central volcano) and building atop of that if you can, the way up only allows for smaller dinos, so you won't have a T-Rex at your door, and if you have turrets? No birds either, you're too much of a hassle to be raided.
-2|0@playark^1438838967#ctt9z12:TelFiRE$:Loss is inevitable, so why build walls? You literally have the same protection if you just put your boxes out in the open and pin code. Anyone who wants to break them, can. Built a base? Doesn't matter. Anyone who wants to break everything you own, can. Made of metal? Doesn't matter. I guess a vault is the only exception to this. Regardless, you and others are missing the point. I was expecting to get raided, and have no problem losing everything. It's the fact that they never even breached that gets to me. They just broke all my shit right through the walls. Knowing that, there is really no safe base you can build. That is completely and utterly gamebreaking, and I do indeed feel the game is pointless to play until that's fixed.
