1|0@playark^1438841479#cttavpr:JasePearson$:I'm currently in the middle of a tribe war, so yes, I know exactly how big a T-Rex is, exactly how large the attack area is. I know why my buildings still have their shit inside them despite being hit by a tribe and why the enemy has no chests left after our T-Rexs went at theirs. It doesn't have to be super tool, just tall enough the T-Rex can't stand on it and with walls wide enough so that it cannot attack and hit your main structure within the structure. Or better yet, find a location that's inaccessible to the larger animals, there's quite a few :) Then you've just gotta defend from raiders with C4. But yeah, I get it, about the EA and it needing to be on their radar, It's just never bothered me as I like to build tall builds in inaccessible locations, although I was amused that we could chomp through a metal base and kill somebody, I figured they'd fix it with dinos being able to clip through walls. 
