1|0@playark^1438819048#ctsz8vv:BitStompr$:That really sucks, but it is avoidable. Our "real base" is a 2x2 box surrounded by stone 2 blocks wide and honeycombed walls. An attacker should never be on the other side of one wall from you, but should be stopped at least 4 blocks before your loot room. Dino will clip through and destroy everything, you need to plan for that. The good news is that it is possible to fend off an attack, you just need to build smart and compact with many layers. This makes having a lot of dinos or a big yard/castle difficult but it's worth it. Look into classic castles vs keeps and you'll see a distinct difference in style. Midevil fortification techniques and building practices apply very well to the ark environment.
